# Commit + push for Vercel verification

The user **never verifies locally**. They only check work via the **Vercel deployment** on phone browsers (Safari/Chrome).

When the user asks to **commit**, **commit and push**, or **commit to main**:

1. Create the git commit as usual.
2. **Immediately push to `origin/main`** (or the current tracking branch if they specified another). Do not stop after a local-only commit.
3. Confirm the push succeeded and remind them Vercel needs a minute to redeploy; hard-refresh if the old UI still appears.

Do not treat "commit" as local-only for this project unless the user explicitly says **local only** or **do not push**.
